\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. When, His salvation bringing,
\par To Zion Jesus came,
\par The children all stood singing
\par Hosanna to His name;
\par Nor did their zeal offend Him,
\par But, as He rode along,
\par He let them still attend Him,
\par And smiled to hear their song.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. And, since the Lord retaineth
\par His love for children still,
\par Though now as King He reigneth
\par On Zion's heavenly hill,
\par We'll flock around His banner
\par Who sits upon the throne,
\par And cry aloud: Hossana
\par To David's royal Son!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. For, should we fall proclaiming
\par Our great Redeemer's praise,
\par The stones, our silence shaming,
\par Would their hosannas raise.
\par But shall we only render
\par The tribute of our words?
\par No! while our hearts are tender,
\par They too shall be the Lord's.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

